# Craft's materials are chosen once the mana is paid (CR 601.2g-h). Deadly Dispute (sacrificing Cecil, Dark Knight, no artifact)
# makes a Treasure. On turn seven Dire Flail crafts with the Treasure as the only other artifact Bot1 has anywhere: the Treasure
# sacrificed for the mana ceases to exist (CR 111.7), so nothing is left to exile and the activation is taken back (CR
# 602.2b, 601.2h) - the Flail, the Treasure and the lands stay as they were. On turn nine, with a second Ornithopter on the
# battlefield, the Treasure pays for the craft again and the Ornithopter is the material: the Treasure is nowhere, the
# Ornithopter alone in exile.

[Bot1 Deck]
Swamp
Dire Flail
Deadly Dispute
Cecil, Dark Knight
Mountain
Mountain
Mountain
Island
Island
Ornithopter
Mountain
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

